// The EMIT config. `npm run build` (and therefore the Dockerfile) compiles with THIS file; the root
// tsconfig.json stays the CHECK config and keeps `include: ["src"]` with no exclude.
//
// Why two files instead of one exclude in the root: `npm run typecheck`, CI, and
// .claude/hooks/typecheck.sh all run `tsc --noEmit` against the ROOT config. Putting these excludes
// there would silently stop type-checking 147 test/fixture/conformance files — the tests would still
// RUN (vitest has its own resolution) but a type error in one would no longer be caught by any gate.
// The check must stay wide and the emit must stay narrow, so the two configs must diverge.
// Mutation that proves the split holds: a type error in any *.test.ts reds `npm run typecheck` and
// does NOT red `npm run build`.
//
// What is excluded and why each pattern is needed:
//   *.test.ts / *.fixtures.ts / *.conformance.ts — test bodies, canned provider payloads, and the
//     per-connector conformance fixture modules. None is imported by production code (verified).
//   src/sdk/conformance.ts — the Vitest-integrating conformance HARNESS. It `import`s "vitest", a
//     devDependency the runner image does not install (`npm ci --omit=dev`), so shipping it put a
//     module in dist/ that could only ever throw MODULE_NOT_FOUND.
//   src/sdk/index.ts — the SDK barrel. It RE-EXPORTS ./conformance.js, and `exclude` does not stop
//     tsc emitting a file that an included file imports: leaving the barrel in would drag the
//     harness back into dist/ regardless of the line above. Nothing outside *.conformance*.ts and
//     *.test.ts imports the barrel (verified by grep over src/, apps/, scripts/), so dropping it
//     from the emit costs the runtime nothing. `src/sdk/contract.ts` — the types real connectors
//     import — is NOT excluded and still compiles.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "exclude": [
    "src/**/*.test.ts",
    "src/**/*.fixtures.ts",
    "src/**/*.conformance.ts",
    "src/sdk/conformance.ts",
    "src/sdk/index.ts"
  ]
}
